IMPORT prelude

-- Central Provident Fund Act 1953 (Singapore) -- the contribution rates for citizens and second-year-plus permanent residents
-- (First Schedule paragraphs 1 and 7, from 1 January 2026), and what happens to CPF moneys on a member's death (s 24(3A),
-- s 25(5)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 1 July 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CPFA1953.txt. First Schedule paragraph 1 as amended by S 886/2025 wef 1 January 2026.
--
-- WHY. Added on 11 October 2026 for two requirements in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl, both raised by the
-- cradle-to-grave-simone scenario: REQ-0001 (event e041: the employer's and employee's shares for an employee aged 23 earning
-- $4,200 in August 2026) and REQ-0012 (event e088: whether CPF moneys paid under a nomination form part of the estate).
--
-- THE FIRST SCHEDULE TABLES ARE COLUMN-SHIFTED IN THE .txt DEPOSIT, as in the Stamp Duties deposit: each band's percentages
-- were read from the cells in order. The second column is the TOTAL the employer pays to the Fund; the third column is the
-- part the employer may recover from the employee's wages.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: additional wages and the annual additional-wage ceiling (the encoding takes ordinary wages only, with no
-- additional wages in the month); the graduated rates for the first two years of permanent residence (paragraphs 1A to 1D);
-- foreign employees; public-sector employees (paragraph 7 and its Regulations); platform workers; the allocation into the
-- Ordinary, Special and Medisave Accounts (s 13 and regulations, REQ-0002); months before January 2026.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Central Provident Fund Act 1953 -- contribution rates and death`

§§ `First Schedule paragraph 1 -- the rates from 1 January 2026`

-- Para 1: "with effect from 1 January 2026, the contributions payable by the employer and the amount recoverable from the
-- employee's wages are as follows", by age band:
--   (a) 55 and below:          wages over $50 to $500: 17% of Total Wages, nothing recoverable;
--                              over $500 to $750: 17% of Total Wages + 0.6 x (Total Wages - $500), of which 0.6 x (Total
--                              Wages - $500) recoverable; over $750: 37% of ordinary wages (capped at 37% of the Ordinary Wage
--                              Ceiling), of which 20% (capped at 20% of the Ceiling) recoverable.
--   (b) above 55 to 60:        16% / 0.54 / 34% of which 18%;
--   (c) above 60 to 65:        12.5% / 0.375 / 25% of which 12.5%;
--   (d) above 65 to 70:        9% / 0.225 / 16.5% of which 7.5%;
--   (e) above 70:              7.5% / 0.15 / 12.5% of which 5%.
-- Wages of $50 or less: no band applies, so no contribution.
DECLARE Band HAS
    `low rate` IS A NUMBER
    `phase-in factor` IS A NUMBER
    `total rate` IS A NUMBER
    `employee rate` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Band
`the rate band for` age MEANS
    IF age AT MOST 55 THEN Band WITH `low rate` IS 0.17, `phase-in factor` IS 0.6, `total rate` IS 0.37, `employee rate` IS 0.2
    ELSE IF age AT MOST 60 THEN Band WITH `low rate` IS 0.16, `phase-in factor` IS 0.54, `total rate` IS 0.34, `employee rate` IS 0.18
         ELSE IF age AT MOST 65 THEN Band WITH `low rate` IS 0.125, `phase-in factor` IS 0.375, `total rate` IS 0.25, `employee rate` IS 0.125
              ELSE IF age AT MOST 70 THEN Band WITH `low rate` IS 0.09, `phase-in factor` IS 0.225, `total rate` IS 0.165, `employee rate` IS 0.075
                   ELSE Band WITH `low rate` IS 0.075, `phase-in factor` IS 0.15, `total rate` IS 0.125, `employee rate` IS 0.05

-- Para 7(ea): the "Ordinary Wage Ceiling" is $6,300 a month for September to December 2023, $6,800 in 2024, $7,400 in 2025, and
-- "$8,000" for "each month in the year 2026 and every subsequent year".
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Ordinary Wage Ceiling in` year MEANS
    IF year AT LEAST 2026 THEN 8000
    ELSE IF year EQUALS 2025 THEN 7400
         ELSE IF year EQUALS 2024 THEN 6800
              ELSE 6300

-- Para 7(b): "the contribution payable by the employer is to be rounded off to the nearest dollar except, where the fraction of a
-- dollar is 50 cents, it is to be regarded as a dollar". (c): "in calculating the amount recoverable by the employer from the
-- employee's wages, a fraction of a dollar is to be ignored".
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest dollar, 50 cents up` x MEANS FLOOR (x PLUS 0.5)

GIVEN wages IS A NUMBER, year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the capped ordinary wages` wages year MEANS
    IF wages GREATER THAN `the Ordinary Wage Ceiling in` year THEN `the Ordinary Wage Ceiling in` year ELSE wages

GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, wages IS A NUMBER, year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total contribution before rounding` age wages year MEANS
    IF wages AT MOST 50 THEN 0
    ELSE IF wages AT MOST 500 THEN wages TIMES (`the rate band for` age)'s `low rate`
         ELSE IF wages AT MOST 750
              THEN wages TIMES (`the rate band for` age)'s `low rate` PLUS (wages MINUS 500) TIMES (`the rate band for` age)'s `phase-in factor`
              ELSE `the capped ordinary wages` wages year TIMES (`the rate band for` age)'s `total rate`

GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, wages IS A NUMBER, year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the employee share before rounding` age wages year MEANS
    IF wages AT MOST 500 THEN 0
    ELSE IF wages AT MOST 750 THEN (wages MINUS 500) TIMES (`the rate band for` age)'s `phase-in factor`
         ELSE `the capped ordinary wages` wages year TIMES (`the rate band for` age)'s `employee rate`

-- The total the employer pays to the Fund for the month.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, wages IS A NUMBER, year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total CPF contribution` age wages year MEANS
    `rounded to the nearest dollar, 50 cents up` (`the total contribution before rounding` age wages year)

-- The part the employer may deduct from the employee's wages.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, wages IS A NUMBER, year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the employee's CPF share` age wages year MEANS
    FLOOR (`the employee share before rounding` age wages year)

-- What the employer bears itself.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, wages IS A NUMBER, year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the employer's own CPF share` age wages year MEANS
    `the total CPF contribution` age wages year MINUS `the employee's CPF share` age wages year

§§ `First Schedule paragraph 7(a) -- when an older band starts`

-- Para 7(a): contributions for an employee "above 55, 60, 65 or 70 years of age are payable -- (i) from the first day of the month
-- following the month in which the employee attains that age; and (ii) in the case of an employee who is born on 29 February,
-- from the first day of March in the year in which the employee attains that age". So the band for a month is fixed by the age
-- the employee had at the end of the PREVIOUS month. The encoding takes "age for the month" as that input.
GIVEN `age at the end of the previous month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the age that sets the month's band` `age at the end of the previous month` MEANS `age at the end of the previous month`

§§ `24(3A), 25(5) -- CPF moneys on death`

-- s 24(3A): "all moneys paid out of the Fund on or after the death of any member of the Fund are deemed to be impressed with a
-- trust in favour of -- (a) the person or persons nominated under section 25(1) by the deceased member, if any; or (b) the person
-- or persons who are entitled to the whole or a share of the moneys payable to the Public Trustee under section 25A(1), but,
-- without affecting the operation of the Estate Duty Act 1929, are deemed not to form part of the deceased member's estate or to
-- be subject to his or her debts."
-- s 25(5): "Any nomination made by a member of the Fund under subsection (1) is revoked -- (a) by his or her marriage ... ; or
-- (b) in such other circumstances ... as the Board may prescribe."
--
-- REQ-0012 asked a case-law question; the Act answers it. CPF moneys paid on death are NOT part of the estate the executor
-- administers, whether paid under a nomination or through the Public Trustee, and are not subject to the member's debts. A will
-- leaving "everything" to the spouse does not reach them. But a nomination made BEFORE the member married is revoked by the
-- marriage, so the moneys go through the Public Trustee route instead (s 25A, not encoded).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `CPF moneys paid on death form part of the member's estate` IF FALSE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `CPF moneys paid on death are subject to the member's debts` IF FALSE

GIVEN `nomination made` IS A BOOLEAN, `member married after the nomination` IS A BOOLEAN, `revoked by the Board's prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the nomination is in force at death` IF
        `nomination made`
    AND (NOT `member married after the nomination`)
    AND (NOT `revoked by the Board's prescribed circumstances`)

GIVEN `nomination made` IS A BOOLEAN, `member married after the nomination` IS A BOOLEAN, `revoked by the Board's prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
`who the CPF moneys are held on trust for` `nomination made` `member married after the nomination` `revoked by the Board's prescribed circumstances` MEANS
    IF `the nomination is in force at death` `nomination made` `member married after the nomination` `revoked by the Board's prescribed circumstances`
    THEN "the nominee"
    ELSE "the persons entitled through the Public Trustee under section 25A"
